# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Virtual environments
.venv/
venv/
env/

# VS Code
.vscode/

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# JVM crash diagnostics - hs_err_pid<N>.log and its matching replay_pid<N>.log
# are dumped wherever the crashing JVM's working directory happened to be
# (seen both at the repo root and under mobile/android/, depending on
# whether it was a Gradle daemon or Android Studio's own JVM that crashed).
# Always local debugging noise, never something to commit.
hs_err_pid*.log
replay_pid*.log

# Scratch files from AI coding assistants / remote computer-use tooling -
# never intended to be committed, just a defensive backstop in case one is
# ever left behind in the working tree.
_claude_*.bat
_claude_*.txt

# Satellite storage - Photo's and Music's own library data, and the Locked
# Folder's PIN hash when explicitly configured to live inside the checkout
# rather than StarCore's application-data directory (the default location
# for a fresh install - see docs/deployment.md, "Runtime data location").
# Kept as a defensive backstop either way: this should normally be empty by
# default, not something relied on to keep secrets out of Git.
satellites/*/*/data/

# Credentials, sessions and TLS material - never committed. By default none
# of this lives inside the checkout at all any more (see runtime_paths.py
# and docs/deployment.md), but engine/data/ is kept ignored as a backstop for
# the historical location (pre-migration, or if migration ever fails and
# falls back to it) and for any advanced setup that points STARCORE_DATA_DIR
# back inside the checkout on purpose.
engine/data/
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.p12
*.pfx

# Machine-specific configuration - the engine's own bind address/port/HTTPS
# paths, and each Satellite's own settings (a Locked Folder path, a photo or
# music library location, a sync port, ...). This is what an installation
# actually edits, so it must never be committed - the tracked config.default.toml
# right beside it (a different filename, so this pattern never matches it -
# see test_gitignore.py) is the schema/shipped-defaults a future StarCore
# version adds a new setting to, read once to fill in anything this
# installation's own config.toml is missing, and never overwritten by it.
# See docs/deployment.md, "Keeping configuration up to date". An existing
# checkout that already has these tracked from before this exists needs one
# `git rm --cached` to stop tracking them - see that same section for the
# exact command.
config.toml

# ---------- mobile/ (the React Native app - see mobile/README.md) ----------

# JS/Node
mobile/node_modules/
mobile/npm-debug.log*
mobile/yarn-error.log*
mobile/.env
mobile/.env.local

# Android build output and local, machine-specific Gradle/SDK settings -
# never anything the app's own source or configuration, all of which stays
# under mobile/android/*/src/ and is unaffected by any of this.
mobile/android/local.properties
mobile/android/.gradle/
mobile/android/build/
mobile/android/app/build/
mobile/android/*.iml
mobile/android/.idea/

# Android signing - a release keystore and its passwords/store are exactly
# the kind of server-specific-equivalent secret this repository must never
# hold (see README.md, "Release builds"); debug builds need no keystore of
# their own at all (see android/app/build.gradle), so nothing legitimate is
# ever named like this.
mobile/android/**/*.keystore
mobile/android/**/*.jks
mobile/android/keystore.properties

# iOS - not part of this block (Android-first; see mobile/README.md), but
# ignored ahead of time so adding the platform later never risks a signing
# certificate, provisioning profile, or Xcode's own local user state
# landing in a commit by accident.
mobile/ios/build/
mobile/ios/Pods/
mobile/ios/*.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
mobile/ios/*.xcodeproj/xcuserdata/
mobile/ios/*.xcodeproj/project.xcworkspace/xcuserdata/
mobile/**/*.mobileprovision
mobile/**/*.p8
mobile/**/*.p12
mobile/**/*.cer

# Metro/React Native caches and editor state - regenerated on demand, never
# something to commit or to diff against.
mobile/.metro-health-check*
mobile/*.log
mobile/.vscode/
mobile/.idea/
